Write a one-page risk assessment memo for a fictional 20-person accounting firm. Identify its five most important information assets, list two threats per asset with the vulnerabilities each exploits, and score likelihood × impact. Recommend one treatment per top-three risk with a rough cost estimate (free, cheap, expensive). Close with the residual risk statement the firm's owner would sign. Deliverable: a single PDF or markdown page, plain language, no unexplained jargon.

