On a Linux lab VM, build a miniature RBAC system. 1) Create two users (analyst1, analyst2) and a group (soc). 2) Create /srv/cases owned by root:soc with mode 2770 and confirm analyst1 can write while an outsider cannot. 3) Add analyst1 to sudo with a single allowed command via visudo (e.g. systemctl restart). 4) Log in as each user and record which actions succeed and which are denied. 5) Write a one-paragraph mapping: which layer (identification, authentication, authorization, accountability) did each step exercise, and where would MFA slot in?

