Build a mini risk register for a fictional small-business web store. 1) List 6 assets (customer database, payment page, admin laptop, backups, email, Wi-Fi). 2) For each, name one realistic threat and one vulnerability. 3) Score likelihood and impact 1-5 and multiply for an inherent risk score. 4) Propose one control per row, re-score residual risk, and pick a treatment (mitigate, accept, avoid, transfer). 5) Write a 3-sentence executive summary naming the top two risks and what you recommend. Use a spreadsheet; keep the math visible so an interviewer can follow it.

