Triage like an L1 analyst using sample data. 1) Take five mock alerts (impossible-travel login, malware hash match, port scan, failed logins x50, odd PowerShell). 2) For each, write: the raw evidence you would pull first, two enrichment questions (who owns the asset? is the user traveling?), and your disposition (true positive, false positive, benign, escalate). 3) Draft a three-line escalation note for the one you escalate to L2. 4) Finally, write one SIEM correlation rule in plain English that would have caught your true positive earlier. Time yourself: triage is a timed discipline.

