Write a one-page SOC runbook for a 'suspected phishing with credential entry' alert. Include: trigger conditions, the first five evidence-gathering steps in order, decision points (when to escalate to L2, when to close as benign), containment actions L1 is authorized to take (disable account, block sender domain), and the documentation fields every ticket must carry. Add a short tuning note: what would you change if this alert fired 200 times a day with 95% false positives? Deliverable: the runbook as a PDF.

